{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792836273,"nonce":"Dv3P0XvitHfFxgH0TKE0dWIJvtg=","title":"A host cannot reserve object room before it registers classes","message":"Hot reload asks the runtime for spare object bytes (hlp_set_object_room) when the reload context is made, in enable_reload / enable_tiered with hot_reload. An embedding host registers its classes first and the interpreter lays them out to verify them, so the request is refused and every run prints the 'classes were laid out before reload was enabled' warning; a reload cannot then add fields to any class.\n\nA host cannot reverse the order: enable_reload needs the interpreter, and the interpreter is where host classes are registered.\n\nProposed: a public ash_core::reload::reserve_object_room() -\u003e bool that a host calls before HLInterpreter::new, reading ASH_RELOAD_ROOM / OBJECT_ROOM as request_object_room does; and request_object_room treats a nonzero hlp_object_room() as already granted instead of asking again and warning. Requested by the caribou session.","files":null}]}